td char="(" align="char">5.08 (2.58, 2.50)</td><td char="." align="char">0.2579</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>Part I shows mean, mean after bias correction, mean of the bootstrap standard error, non-coverage percentage of 95% BC<sub><italic>a</italic></sub> bootstrap confidence intervals (with left and right non-coverage percentages), and mean length of the interval. Part II shows, for <italic>p</italic><sub>gs</sub>&#x000a0;&#x02264;&#x000a0;0.3, the same type of results as part I, but for <inline-formula id="IEq203"><!-- Alternate image not processed: 122_2009_1047_Article_IEq203.gif --><tex-math id="M106">\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}\usepackage{amsmath}\usepackage{wasysym} \usepackage{amsfonts} \usepackage{amssymb} \usepackage{amsbsy}\usepackage{mathrsfs}\usepackage{upgreek}\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}\begin{document}$$ D_{{\bar{L}}}^{\rm mod}$$\end{document}</tex-math></inline-formula> truncated at zero. Instead of means, medians are given. At <italic>p</italic><sub>gs</sub>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;0.0, only non-coverage at the right of <italic>p</italic><sub>gs</sub>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;0.0 is considered</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="Tab3"><label>Table&#x000a0;3</label><caption><p>Results from a simulation study on <inline-formula id="IEq206"><!-- Alternate image not processed: 122_2009_1047_Article_IEq206.gif --><tex-math id="M107">\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}\usepackage{amsmath}\usepackage{wasysym} \usepackage{amsfonts} \usepackage{amssymb} \usepackage{amsbsy}\usepackage{mathrsfs}\usepackage{upgreek}\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}\begin{document}$$ D_{L}^{\rm mod} $$\end{document}</tex-math></inline-formula> for a range of values of genetic similarity <italic>p</italic><sub>gs</sub> and expected numbers of fragments <italic>m</italic><sub>1</sub> and <italic>m</italic><sub>2,</sub> 10,000 replicated pairs of AFLP profiles, 1,000 bootstrap resamples, <italic>fld</italic><italic>F</italic><sub><italic>S</italic></sub> from <italic>A. thaliana</italic> with <italic>N</italic>&#x000a0;=&#x000a0;450</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="2" colspan="3">Parameter settings</th><th align="left" colspan="5">Part I Results for <inline-formula id="IEq208"><!-- Alternate image not processed: 122_2009_1047_Article_IEq208.gif --><tex-math id="M108">\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}\usepackage{amsmath}\usepackage{wasysym} \usepackage{amsfonts} \usepackage{amssymb} \usepackage{amsbsy}\usepackage{mathrsfs}\usepackage{upgreek}\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}\begin{document}$$ D_{L}^{\rm mod} $$\end{document}</tex-math></inline-formula></th></tr><tr><th align="left" colspan="3">Mean and SE</th><th align="left" colspan="2">95% BC<sub><italic>a</italic></sub> bootstrap ci</th></tr><tr><th align="left"><italic>p</italic><sub>gs</sub></th><th align="left"><italic>m</italic><sub><italic>1</italic></sub></th><th align="left"><italic>m</italic><sub><italic>2</italic></sub></th><th align="left">Mean</th><th align="left">Mean after bias correction</th><th align="left">Bootstrap SE</th><th align="left">Non-coverage % (too low, too high)</th><th align="left">Length</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">0.0</td><td char="." align="char">40</td><td char="." align="char">40</td><td char="." align="char">&#x02212;0.0009</td><td char="." align="char">&#x02212;0.0008</td><td char="." align="char">0.0651</td><td char="(" align="char">5.55 (3.15, 2.40)</td><td char="." align="char">0.2605</td></tr><tr><td align="left"/><td char="." align="char">70</td><td char="." align="char">70</td><td char="." align="char">&#x02212;0.0017</td><td char="." align="char">&#x02212;0.0014</td><td char="." align="char">0.0698</td><td char="(" align="char">5.17 (2.68, 2.49)</td><td char="." align="char">0.2725</td></tr><tr><td align="left"/><td char="." align="char">120</td><td char="." align="char">120</td><td char="." align="char">&#x02212;0.0021</td><td char="." align="char">&#x02212;0.00